Summary: Don't hold the Mac driver's window lock across WM_SIZING
Category: input
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/)
Why: During a live resize the Mac driver asks the program about each new
 size (query_resize_size, WM_SIZING). It sent WM_SIZING while holding its
 process-wide window data lock (get_win_data), which every GL present also
 takes (macdrv_client_surface_update and _present). A program whose WM_SIZING
 handler waits for its renderer thread, while that thread holds the
 program's own lock and presents, deadlocks both threads for good, and the
 resize query is never answered. Now the driver copies the window's rects
 and releases the lock before sending WM_SIZING.
Programs: Old Clock under cnc-ddraw (OpenGL renderer) in Second Chance's
 host (app-embedded protocol, 2026-11-28): the first live resize hung the
 game's window thread and its renderer, with no resize_size_reply and no
 frames after it.
Uncertain: Seen only through a host; the plain driver's windowWillResize:toSize:
 sends the same query, so it should hang the same way, but that hasn't been
 shown.
No test: needs a live resize driven from macOS or a host; reproduced with
 tools/wmh-testhost (WMH_TESTHOST_RESIZE=1) and a window whose WM_SIZING
 waits for a GL thread that presents twice under the same lock
Status: 11.19-11.21: 2026-11-28: ported from 11.22 (plain driver context, no
 winemac-host-windows); window.c compile-checked with clang -fsyntax-only on
 each version.
 11.21, 11.20: 2026-11-28: macfixes build2 of each (host builds, meeka,
 from acc62fe): smoke passed; suite 60 and 52 passed, 3 skipped, 0 failed.
 Live resize not rerun on them.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -2140,14 +2140,19 @@
 bool query_resize_size(HWND hwnd, macdrv_query *query)
 {
     struct macdrv_win_data *data = get_win_data(hwnd);
+    struct window_rects rects;
     RECT rect;
     int corner;
     bool ret = false;
 
     if (!data) return false;
+    /* Not held across WM_SIZING: a program's handler may wait for its own
+     * thread that is presenting GL, which takes this lock too. */
+    rects = data->rects;
+    release_win_data(data);
 
     rect = rect_from_cgrect(query->resize_size.rect);
-    rect = window_rect_from_visible(&data->rects, rect);
+    rect = window_rect_from_visible(&rects, rect);
 
     if (query->resize_size.from_left)
     {
@@ -2163,12 +2168,11 @@
 
     if (send_message(hwnd, WM_SIZING, corner, (LPARAM)&rect))
     {
-        rect = visible_rect_from_window(&data->rects, rect);
+        rect = visible_rect_from_window(&rects, rect);
         query->resize_size.rect = cgrect_from_rect(rect);
         ret = true;
     }
 
-    release_win_data(data);
     return ret;
 }
 
